final_entries.prompt:
My CSS sidebar is not staying fixed on the right side of the page. It scrolls with the content. Here is my CSS:

.sidebar {
    width: 250px;
    position: relative;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
}

How do I make it stay visible while scrolling?

final_entries.response:
The problem is position: relative. Relative positioning does not remove the element from the document flow - it just offsets it visually. To make an element stay fixed while scrolling, use position: fixed:

.sidebar {
    width: 250px;
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 100vh;
    overflow-y: auto;
}

Key changes:
1. Changed relative to fixed - this pins the element to the viewport
2. Added height: 100vh so it spans the full viewport height
3. Added overflow-y: auto so if the sidebar content is taller than the viewport, users can scroll within the sidebar itself
